\section{Distributions of Patents and Trademarks by Firm Age}

The average number of patents and trademarks per firm increases with age, while the average number per worker decreases with age in both the BR and PC sets of firms. Firms in the PC set have a higher average number of patents and trademarks per firm than those in the BR set. However, the number per worker is lower, probably due to higher average employment in PC firms.

