Patenting without introducing new products in the previous two years is correlated with a higher likelihood of being a high growth young firm for small and medium firms. Patenting without introducing new products in the previous two years is correlated with an additional 3,9\% employment growth and 5,5\% employment growth for large firms. Dropping product lines is correlated with a lower likelihood of being a high growth young firm for large firms and a 12,9\% lower employment growth rate.  Other variables are not significant or are not robust to including industry and time fixed effects.


