\section{Product Decisions of Mature Superstar Firms}
To capture the relation between firm growth and the product decisions of high-growth young firms, we run the following regression:
    
\[
Y_{ikt} =  \beta^N D^N_{ik\hat{t}} + \beta^X D^X_{ik\hat{t}} + \sum_{I \in \{P, TM\}} \left( \beta^I D^I_{ik\hat{t}} + \beta^{I \times N} \left( D^I_{ik\hat{t}} \times D^N_{ik\hat{t}} \right) \right) \times D^{SS}_{ikt} + X_{ik\hat{t}} + \alpha_k + \alpha_t + \varepsilon_{ik\hat{t}}.
\]

Superstar firms are significatly more responsive in employment growth when they have patented and introduced new products at the same time. This possitive correlation is present and significant among medium and large firms. However, this differential correlation is not significant in revenue growth.

